# Suppressions for sc_test_ctime (valgrind memcheck). Each names one branch
# whose outcome is public by design; nothing here may hide a branch on a key.
#
# libsodium 1.0.22, crypto_aead/xchacha20poly1305/aead_xchacha20poly1305.c,
# _decrypt_detached (inlined into the public function): after the constant-
# time crypto_verify_16 of the tag, `if (ret != 0)` clears the output and
# returns -1. Whether a tag verified is what every caller learns anyway.
# Two forms: with debug information valgrind shows the inlined frame.
{
   xchacha20poly1305-tag-check-outcome-inlined
   Memcheck:Cond
   fun:_decrypt_detached
   fun:crypto_aead_xchacha20poly1305_ietf_decrypt_detached
   fun:crypto_aead_xchacha20poly1305_ietf_decrypt
   fun:sc_unseal
}
{
   xchacha20poly1305-tag-check-outcome
   Memcheck:Cond
   fun:crypto_aead_xchacha20poly1305_ietf_decrypt_detached
   fun:crypto_aead_xchacha20poly1305_ietf_decrypt
   fun:sc_unseal
}
